    ├── Used APIs  : attr.s, attr.ib
    ├── Pitfalls   : dataclasses uses @dataclass decorator instead of @attr.s; dataclasses.field() 
    │   replaces attr.ib() with slightly different parameters (default_factory vs factory); attr.ib() 
    │   supports validators and converters which require __post_init__ in dataclasses; attr provides 
    │   slots=True by default in newer versions; dataclasses requires explicit slots=True parameter 
    │   (Python 3.10+)
    └── The code uses attr.s as a class decorator and attr.ib for field definition with type annotations. 
        Python's standard library dataclasses provides equivalent functionality with @dataclass decorator 
        and field() function, making it a direct drop-in replacement for this usage pattern.

